- **null.go** (`NullUUID`, the SQL Scan/Value wrapper): Samuel Roth holds 91 lines (90.1%), 107 counting blanks (90.7%), all from one commit in 2021.

None of the authors of any SQL file has committed in the last year. The most recent of them was Andrew Stone, in 2017. There is no active person to consult, so whoever reviews these is effectively doing it fresh.

## What I'd do
- **v7 changes:** ask Mei Chen to review, and try MikeWang as the original author if you can reach them.
- **time.go changes:** ask Alexander Rowe, and also review v7-related parts with Mei Chen.
- **SQL changes:** you'll be the de facto owner. Lean on `sql_test.go` and `null_test.go` (Samuel Roth wrote 198 lines there).
- **Ask Ravi Menon** about current project conventions. They're the most recently active committer.

## Caveats
- **These counts measure whose code survives, not who understands it.** Review comments and design discussions don't show up in line counts.
- **Possible duplicate identities are not merged.** The repo-wide summary flags these as likely the same person, based only on names and email addresses. That's a guess, nobody has confirmed it, and I haven't applied it.
  - **Paul Borman** has three addresses. Counted as one person, he'd hold 1,201 lines (41.7%) of the whole repo, against 1,135 (39.5%) for the <email redacted> address alone.
  - **Alex Rowe** has two addresses, holding 63 lines (alex@rowe.example) and 19 lines (alex.rowe@mailbox.example). That would be 82 lines (2.9%) if they're one person. I also haven't confirmed that "Alex Rowe" is the same person as "Alexander Rowe" in time.go.
